WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.260
- You actually grew up with
quite a bit of obstacles.

00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:03.093
What happened?

00:00:03.093 --> 00:00:05.630
- I mean, one of my biggest hurdles

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:06.730
growing up in middle school,

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:09.260
I wore a back brace for two and
a half years, like you know,

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:11.410
those Romy and Michelle ones.
- In middle school?

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:13.093
- Yeah, seventh and eighth grade.

00:00:13.093 --> 00:00:14.390
- Middle school already sucks.

00:00:14.390 --> 00:00:16.220
- It was rough (laughs).
- Wow.

00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:17.937
- It was rough, and the doctor was like,

00:00:17.937 --> 00:00:19.850
"If you don't wear this,
you won't be able to dance."

00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:22.700
So I was like, I have to
dance, I love dancing.

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:25.050
So my mom and I, we went to Macy's,

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:27.540
I bought clothes to go over my back brace,

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:30.350
and I just embraced the brace,

00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:31.183
(audience laughing)

00:00:31.183 --> 00:00:36.177
and I'd be like, "Punch my
stomach, it's hard as a rock."

00:00:36.177 --> 00:00:37.706
(audience laughing)
- See this is where

00:00:37.706 --> 00:00:39.170
your personality came in.

00:00:39.170 --> 00:00:42.130
- Yeah, and so that helped
me build my confidence

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:45.630
to just kind of not allow people to,

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:48.290
I don't know, bring me
down or anything like that.

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:51.721
- Or categorize you.
(audience clapping)

00:00:51.721 --> 00:00:52.850
- I think you're a very powerful woman,

00:00:52.850 --> 00:00:54.630
a very powerful presence, and I love that.

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:56.130
And I also know you're very powerful

00:00:56.130 --> 00:00:58.410
because you tried to start your own band

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:00.151
when you were a kid,
but you were too bossy?

00:01:00.151 --> 00:01:03.251
- No, I wasn't, who told you that?

00:01:03.251 --> 00:01:04.640
(audience laughing)

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:05.770
No, here's the thing.

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:08.830
I used my parents' printer,
like all of their ink,

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:10.136
you know very expensive,

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:11.385
(audience laughing)

00:01:11.385 --> 00:01:12.730
and I would print out business cards

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:14.840
for a business I didn't have.

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:16.600
And I was choreographer,

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:18.190
and then I was looking for band mates,

00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:19.829
and I put fliers all over

00:01:19.829 --> 00:01:20.820
the park.
- And no one responded?

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:22.214
- No one called.

00:01:22.214 --> 00:01:23.660
(audience laughing)

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:25.690
And so I pretended--
- I bet they're calling now.

00:01:25.690 --> 00:01:28.078
- They should have answered that flier.

00:01:28.078 --> 00:01:30.457
(audience laughing)
I put up a lot of them.

00:01:30.457 --> 00:01:32.070
(audience clapping)

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:35.840
So yeah, I was a one-person
band for a long time.

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:39.570
It's interesting because my
biggest weakness growing up

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:41.700
was that I was gay,

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:43.890
and that I was different
from everyone else.

00:01:43.890 --> 00:01:46.230
And now it's become my biggest strength

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:50.204
because it's empowered me to--
(audience cheering)

00:01:50.204 --> 00:01:51.163
- I think why?

00:01:51.163 --> 00:01:52.430
Is it because you are who you are?

00:01:52.430 --> 00:01:55.280
- Yeah, and I think I
really feared growing up

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:58.100
because I was like, life is
going to be so difficult,

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:01.020
and people are just not
going to understand.

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:03.520
Going into my music career,

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:07.810
I was just like, if I'm
scared, everyone else will be,

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:10.990
so I have to embrace who I am,
I have to be the brave one,

00:02:10.990 --> 00:02:13.490
because if I take that first step,

00:02:13.490 --> 00:02:14.900
everyone else will follow.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:17.910
And they will hopefully
(audience clapping)

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:21.780
grow to feel inspired and know

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:23.210
that they can have a good life.

00:02:23.210 --> 00:02:24.730
They don't have to commit suicide,

00:02:24.730 --> 00:02:26.470
they don't have to not love themselves,

00:02:26.470 --> 00:02:30.050
they can be loved, and
it's about all these

00:02:30.050 --> 00:02:33.380
incredible, powerful women,
and just people in general,

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:36.810
taking that first step and
initiative to showcase that.

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:37.643
- Absolutely.

